{
  "_note": "Joshua edits this via the UI Layout Editor (visual, native). x/y are offsets in canonical pixels from the anchor corner of a 1280x800 reference frame. The game applies positions defensively at startup; a missing/corrupt file changes nothing. FACES (2026-10-17): this file carries two layout faces under \"faces\" \u2014 \"mobile\" and \"desktop\" \u2014 each with its own full \"elements\" list. The game (ui_layout_apply.js) applies the face matching the screen it runs on and falls back to the other face, then to the top-level \"elements\", when a face is missing. The top-level \"elements\" list is a legacy mirror of the mobile face, kept so older tools keep working. The UI Editor (v1.8.0+) edits one face at a time via its Mobile/Desktop switch and always saves both faces. The mobile face is Joshua's layout exactly as he arranged it; the desktop face started as an exact copy of it.",
